WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.403 --> 00:00:03.553
Unit twenty. Health Communication!

2
00:00:04.521 --> 00:00:09.213
Hello, everyone! I'm Doctor Sokha, your school doctor.

3
00:00:09.263 --> 00:00:12.340
Hi, Doctor Sokha! What do we learn today?

4
00:00:12.390 --> 00:00:16.664
Today we learn about Health Communication. Let's go!

5
00:00:17.826 --> 00:00:22.959
Health communication. Say it with me. Health communication!

6
00:00:26.455 --> 00:00:29.988
Message. Say it with me. Message!

7
00:00:33.487 --> 00:00:37.387
Audience. Say it with me. Audience!

8
00:00:40.889 --> 00:00:44.906
Campaign. Say it with me. Campaign!

9
00:00:48.406 --> 00:00:52.989
Misinformation. Say it with me. Misinformation!

10
00:00:56.443 --> 00:00:59.977
Trust. Say it with me. Trust!

11
00:01:03.517 --> 00:01:07.650
Evidence. Say it with me. Evidence!

12
00:01:11.112 --> 00:01:15.612
Behaviour change. Say it with me. Behaviour change!

13
00:01:19.153 --> 00:01:30.657
Health communication shares clear messages with the right audience. A good campaign uses evidence, builds trust, counters misinformation, and supports behaviour change.

14
00:01:30.707 --> 00:01:34.077
Now I understand. Thank you, Doctor Sokha!

15
00:01:34.815 --> 00:01:40.041
Look! What's the word?

16
00:01:40.091 --> 00:01:41.241
Audience!

17
00:01:42.210 --> 00:01:47.296
Look! What's the word?

18
00:01:47.346 --> 00:01:48.496
Evidence!

19
00:01:49.572 --> 00:01:57.849
Did you know? Messages that show people how to act are often more effective than messages that only frighten them!

20
00:01:57.899 --> 00:02:00.356
Wow! I did not know that!

21
00:02:01.430 --> 00:02:09.269
Think and answer. What makes a health campaign effective?

22
00:02:09.319 --> 00:02:10.469
Great answer!

23
00:02:11.381 --> 00:02:16.998
Great job today! Stay healthy, and see you next time. Goodbye!

24
00:02:17.048 --> 00:02:20.041
Goodbye, everyone! Stay healthy!

